{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/266825-ideas-for-a-new-wraith-game","id":266825,"title":"Ideas for a new Wraith game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-27T10:05:53-07:00","id":266825,"title":"Ideas for a new Wraith game?","content":"A long time ago, I brought most of the Wraith books but I've never really ran a game for it. Since I really liked the setting when I read it, I was interested to see that Wr20 was on the horizon. However, before buying yet more books to sit on my never played pile, I thought since it's a good way off I've got time to actually run a game with the old rules to see if my group like the setting.<br /> <br /> I've just starting reading the core book, but while I'm doing that, I wondered if anyone out there had any suggestions for a story involving new wraiths? <br /> <br /> Cheers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3955-roguewind","name":"Roguewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T10:38:03-07:00","id":266851,"title":"","content":"I've only run two Wraith chronicles and been in one Con game. <br /> <br /> The Con game was... decent... There were some people there who really really loved and knew the game. Some more than the people running the game. It was using the Shoah book, so it was a little darker than most Wraith games. I enjoyed the session a lot despite some of the flaws and that was my one chance to play Wraith. If it is something that everyone can agree on, the Dark Kingdom of Wire is a... compelling?... way to get to the heart of some of Wraith's themes with a &quot;do not pass go, do not collect $200&quot; spin. <br /> <br /> One chronicle was really a mini-chronicle that happened as a break during a very long Mage game. The game tied into the plots and some characters from the Mage game from a very different angle. It was such a long game we also had Vampire and Changeling mini-chronicle break-outs, as well. Since we knew it was temporary, it was pretty fun. You didn't have to invest as much. It was a city-based game (St. Louis). A LOT of the important wraiths in the city ended up appearing as living folks later on in the game after a bit of time travel. Overall, very good.<br /> <br /> The other was a city-based long-running single arc Wraith game. We had to deal with a lot more of actually making the game and setting work and jibe. We didn't do anything with the Labyrinth, the Tempest (except for Argos and Harrowings) or the government of Stygia except as distant-on-the-horizon figures. It went very well from start to finish with all the character Wraith trimmings (some great Shadowguiding, delicious Harrowings - the players were used to taking parts in each others Seekings, it was fun for them to be less positive and get to do the same thing... plus, easier for me, since I would let the character in question's Shadowguide take over &quot;directing&quot; the Harrowing... so less work for me). <br /> <br /> We planned to start Orpheus, but decided against it for some reason I can't remember.<br /> <br /> I would like to play and run in a game that had a little more Shadowlands/Dark Kingdom/Labyrinth-diving. The &quot;other&quot; side of Wraith as it were. Now Wr20 is coming, we'll see....<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T14:09:51-07:00","id":268524,"title":"","content":"You're all victims of the same serial killer. Figure it out from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T14:50:04-07:00","id":268558,"title":"","content":"That was pretty much the &quot;you all died in the same airplane crash&quot; idea. It wasn't just a random airplane crash due to a flaw in some mechanical system, though it was a random flaw that caused the crash, Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T11:09:41-07:00","id":276508,"title":"","content":"You were hit and died in a drunk driving accident. Both you and the drunk driver have to work together to understand and survive this strange new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"